Terms for the text of the Patent Peace License

The Patent Peace License is not licensed under itself. Its text is
offered freely, so that it can be used, improved, and succeeded.

Anyone may copy, distribute, adapt, and build upon the text of the
Patent Peace License, in any version published in this repository,
without permission and without charge, including to apply it to their
own works and to write licenses that improve on it or succeed it.

One condition keeps every adopter certain of the terms they chose: an
adapted text must carry its own name, and must not be presented as a
version of the Patent Peace License published in this repository. A
successor may say that it succeeds the Patent Peace License.

Anyone who writes a successor is invited, but not required, to keep a
provision like Section 13, so that the path of improvement stays open
for everyone who comes after.

The license text is based on the text of the Apache License, Version
2.0, copyright The Apache Software Foundation. It is not the Apache
License and is not endorsed by The Apache Software Foundation.

The other files in this repository, such as the README, may be used
under the same terms.
